new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ff8b0ebb72426ad4f8cfccb7f714a170417316ce
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rclcpp/OHOS_SIGNAL_HANDLING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# OpenHarmony signal handling
+
+On the KaihongOS RK3588A target, ROS must handle SIGINT/SIGTERM gracefully
+without invoking FFRT's terminating fault dispatcher as an ordinary callback.
+The exact previous sigaction remains available for restoration when ROS
+uninstalls its handlers. Ordinary application handlers still receive their
+original one-argument or SA_SIGINFO calling convention.
+
+Two separate problems were found in a real ros2 launch shutdown:
+
+1. Strict C++ compilation on OHOS does not define the POSIX feature macros
+   previously used to select sigaction. The library chose std::signal, then
+   called FFRT's three-argument handler through a one-argument pointer. A real
+   talker crashed at FFRT's siginfo access, address 0x50. The OHOS compiler
+   defines `__OHOS__`, and the SDK exposes sigaction; that platform now selects
+   the correct API explicitly. Default and ignored dispositions are checked
+   even when SA_SIGINFO is set.
+2. Correcting that ABI alone removed the invalid access but did not permit
+   graceful shutdown. The system FFRT dispatcher restores its saved action
+   and requeues the signal, so invoking it manually caused SIGINT termination.
+   Native ELF evidence showed sigaction at offset 0x68e74 and the AArch64
+   rt_tgsigqueueinfo call at 0x68e9c. The inspected system library SHA-256 was
+   `9262fafbfa0d37276beecb2414dddfea710ba201ebf5f18b053c8aebe02f65b1`.
+
+The implementation keeps restored actions separate from chainable callbacks.
+During installation, an OHOS-only helper uses dladdr to recognize the system
+NDK FFRT library paths. That dispatcher is retained for uninstall but omitted
+from the callbacks invoked by ROS. Other handlers remain chainable. Module
+lookup occurs during installation, never inside the signal handler. Fatal
+signals outside the SIGINT/SIGTERM options are unaffected. The GNU declaration
+needed for dladdr is confined to one implementation file.
+
+Native regression evidence (2026-09-07):
+
+- `signal_chain_red2_20260907`: five cases, five failures. Four detected the
+  wrong installed ABI; the legacy-handler case detected a lost signal mask.
+  Archive SHA-256:
+  `129066ddc1d1a21e77ec7914b77ec7a816f3be95c90b6b2fdf1d30daf04d6684`.
+- `signal_chain_green_20260907`: those five cases passed after the sigaction
+  correction, before the real FFRT requeue case was added.
+- `ffrt_chain_red_20260907`: six cases, one failure. The test verified the
+  real system FFRT origin and flags 0x14000004, then died from SIGINT.
+  Archive SHA-256:
+  `9de10c91851f02d6c2d92ee68229d4e5b8b52bd58d442a9904612a0f74a6ba6e`.
+- `ffrt_chain_green_20260907`: all six passed, including restoration of the
+  real FFRT disposition and preservation of ordinary callbacks and masks.
+  READY, terminal, raw log, XML and archive verdicts agree. Archive SHA-256:
+  `5a3e2f2cb3c41ebc232927ac282164227d5be51625b44be8833947e42655f371`.
+
+The tested production library SHA-256 is
+`cde55d5d806eb738c98fbb5c0d34d7e7cb8b5b7b4c41b7141d8507972fa1cd55`.
+Formatting the test source afterwards did not change this library.
+Real two-board launch run `cli_launch_ffrt_fix_20260907` loaded this exact
+private library on both boards, delivered peer samples over DSoftBus, forwarded
+SIGINT from launch, observed native and CLI exit zero, and verified graph
+withdrawal. Its partial CLI manifest SHA-256 is
+`0f5d03fbcf2276eec116f5be4fde97e82ccbecba60ac3c93876d31ac6de15559`.
+The same library also passed the two-board ros2 run process-group shutdown
+regression `cli_run_ffrt_fix_20260907`; its manifest SHA-256 is
+`da912da1e6f7e966067aff26509a35b4401081f0d19ef5bf59806d1f00ea88c2`.
+Fifteen launch and eleven run evidence-adversary checks passed. The four
+changed C++ files pass the workspace's ament_uncrustify check.
+
+This validates the signal fix and its launch integration. It does not claim
+that all rclcpp tests, all ROS CLI/graph cases or a final release gate passed.
+Board-wide shared installation is a separate deployment step; these runtime
+checks use verified private libraries.
